{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_00_M93zM8ly3IV5ZO2UulvS2184","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tCreated-GMT: 2026-11-26 15:18:06 GMT\n2\tCreated-Local: 2026-11-26 10:18:06 EST\n3\tRole: Compiler Engineer (numeric semantics)\n4\tBranch: fix/float-kind-portability (base `7f4898f4`, resumed from WIP `09401506`, uncommitted working tree per orchestrator rule)\n5\tAuthority:\n6\t- `collab/yang-clojure/1795693415000-architect-float-kind-portability-ruling.gpt-6-astra.findings.md` (normative, RULING 1–5)\n7\t- `collab/yang-clojure/1795695531000-engineer-float-kind-portability.prompt.md` (round brief)\n8\t\n9\tImplementers:\n10\t- Status-Event: 2026-11-26 12:58 GMT | Model: glm-5.3 (session 519cc353, darkstar) | Status: superseded | Rationale: owner-directed migration to remote host; drafted Gates 1/2/4/5 test file + JVM pre-fix legacy fixture in `09401506`\n11\t- Status-Event: 2026-11-26 15:18 GMT | Model: gemini-4-neon (linux worktree) | Status: completed | Rationale: captured Node pre-fix legacy fixture, locked full 7-gate RED evidence on JVM+Node, implemented shared numeric-token factory + Clojure token-aware reader + carrier admission + scoped numeric primitives + migration/docs, verified GREEN across all four hosts (JVM, Node, Dart, Jolt) + regression oracles + demo build + `clj-kondo` 0 errors\n12\t\n13\t# Findings: `fix/float-kind-portability` r1 — Lexical Preservation of Clojure Float Literals\n14\t\n15\t## 1. Executive Summary\n16\t\n17\tClojure numeric literal kind preservation from original source text to `dao.jing.cbor` / UAST / VM execution is implemented and verified green across all seven acceptance gates of RULING 5 and all four hosts (JVM, Node, Dart, Jolt), strictly inside RULING 5's file boundaries:\n18\t\n19\t1. **Shared numeric-token factory** (`src/cljc/yang/core/numeric_token.cljc`): single portable token classifier and carrier constructor with per-language dialect tables (`:clojure`, `:typescript`, `:python`, `:php`). TypeScript, Python, and PHP ANTLR lowerers were migrated onto it without changing any existing Python/TS/PHP golden addresses, and a new PHP float producer parity test (`test/yang/php/antlr/float_address_test.cljc`) was added.\n20\t2. **Frontend-owned, token-aware Clojure source reader** (`src/cljc/yang/clojure/reader.cljc`): consumes original Clojure source text directly and materializes numeric tokens through `yang.core.numeric-token/materialize :clojure` **at token time**, before collection construction (`{...}`, `#{...}`) or lowering can lose kind or coalesce `1` and `1.0`. Zero ambient mutable state, no regex-over-source, no postwalk over read `Number`s, no print-round-trip, and no global reader monkeypatch. Supports optional `:file`/`:source-positions?` indexing for `yang.io`.\n21\t3. **Carrier admission & scoped execution reboxing**:\n22\t   - `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc` admits `cbor/float64?`, `cbor/decimal?`, `cbor/ratio?`, and `host-int/big-carrier?` in `literal?` and `constant-form?` (direct, nested, and quoted).\n23\t   - `src/cljc/yang/clojure/numeric.cljc` exports carrier-aware Clojure numeric primitives (`+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`, kind-strict `=` via `data/equiv`, cross-kind `==`, `!=`) that route float operations through `yin.vm.float` and rebox float results as `data/float64`. Scoped to `yang.clojure/primitives` via `yin.repl.frontends` — global `yin.vm/primitives`, `dao.jing.cbor`, `yin.vm.data`, and `Float64` `:carrier-coercion` policy are untouched.\n24\t4. **Migration, custody, and documentation** (RULING 3 & RULING 4):\n25\t   - `:yang/clojure` manifest bumped to revision `\"c1-3\"`, lowering profile `:yang.clojure/constructed-collections-float-kind-v1`, support profile `:yang.clojure/c1-float-kind`, grammar capability `:source-text` (JVM/Node) vs `:forms-only` (Dart/Jolt, with honest `:unavailable-on-cljd` / `:unavailable-on-jolt` refusals on direct `read-forms`).\n26\t   - Both genuine pre-fix `c1-2` legacy artifacts (JVM float-bearing + Node integer-bearing) archived under `test/resources/yang/clojure/` and verified loaded, decoded, re-encoded, and executed without recompilation on all four hosts.\n27\t   - Documentation updated in `docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md`, `docs/design/yang.antlr.md` (§8.8.1), `docs/design/yang.preludes.md` (§8.1), `src/cljc/yang/docs/yang_implementation.md`, and `test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc`.\n28\t\n29\t---\n30\t\n31\t## 2. Pre-Fix Legacy Custody Artifacts (Captured Before Production Edits)\n32\t\n33\tCaptured from pre-fix `c1-2` (`7f4898f4` / `09401506`) before modifying any production code; one-shot capture test `test/yang/floatkind_legacy_capture_test.cljc` was subsequently removed.\n34\t\n35\t| Fixture | Host | Size | SHA-256 | Manifest Revision | Canonical Root | Runtime Value |\n36\t|---|---|---:|---|---|---|---|\n37\t| `test/resources/yang/clojure/float-kind-legacy-jvm-float.cbor` | JVM (`:jvm-float`) | 1,415 B | `71dc93298c26773dc8383f5d12e03d732840052692a272c16c4aaf4ec90783ec` | `\"c1-2\"` | `:segment/blake3-7cdae9dfee7f1980ccdd9543f279d0d7d20e4a4a4a44dda14f88f54ba9002049` | `float64(1.0)` |\n38\t| `test/resources/yang/clojure/float-kind-legacy-node-integer.cbor` | Node (`:node-integer`) | 1,390 B | `ffb9db68eb953ccadd681b916a8df6d262206baa055d6f91eda461d179174ef2` | `\"c1-2\"` | `:segment/blake3-541ba2ffc6b74327f70008d2069a35279612c2e96c82cc198d7b0b6782501e4c` | exact integer `1` |\n39\t\n40\t---\n41\t\n42\t## 3. TDD RED Evidence (Locked Before Implementation)\n43\t\n44\tAll RED logs are preserved unmodified under `collab/yang-clojure/1795702210000-floatkind-evidence/`:\n45\t\n46\t| Stage | Host | Command | Result | Log File |\n47\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n48\t| Initial Gates 1/2/4/5 RED | JVM | `clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-float-kind-test` | 18 tests, 180 assertions, **20 failures, 1 error** (`RC=1`) | `collab/yang-clojure/1795702210000-floatkind-evidence/red-jvm-gates1245.log` |\n49\t| Initial Gates 1/2/4/5 RED | Node | `npx shadow-cljs compile test && node target/node-tests.js --test=yang.clojure-float-kind-test` | 17 tests, 163 assertions, **63 failures, 4 errors** (`RC=1`) | `collab/yang-clojure/1795702210000-floatkind-evidence/red-node-gates1245.log` |\n50\t| Complete 7-Gate RED | JVM | `clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-float-kind-test` + `yang.clojure-collection-order-test` (`corpus-cross-host-reference-test`, `unmodified-source-integral-floats-test`) | 21 tests / 228 assertions (**19 failures, 1 error**) + 2 tests / 22 assertions (**2 failures, 0 errors**) (`RC=1`) | `collab/yang-clojure/1795702210000-floatkind-evidence/red-jvm-all7gates.log` |\n51\t| Complete 7-Gate RED | Node | `node target/node-tests.js --test=yang.clojure-float-kind-test,yang.clojure-collection-order-test/corpus-cross-host-reference-test,yang.clojure-collection-order-test/unmodified-source-integral-floats-test` | 22 tests, 214 assertions, **75 failures, 5 errors** (`RC=1`) | `collab/yang-clojure/1795702210000-floatkind-evidence/red-node-all7gates.log` |\n52\t\n53\tKey pre-fix failure modes observed in RED:\n54\t- On Node: `\"0.0\"`, `\"1.0\"`, `\"-1.0\"`, `\"1e0\"`, `\"9007199254740992.0\"`, `\"1e19\"`, `\"2.\"`, `\"1E5\"` all collapsed into exact integers in `cljs.tools.reader` / `cljs.reader`; `\"{1 :a 1.0 :b}\"` and `\"#{1 1.0}\"` coalesced keys/elements during reading; `1/2` and `1M` were refused or misread; REPL arithmetic returned unboxed JS `Number`s; `\"(inc 1.0)\"` took the integer branch; Gate 3 unmodified-source `\"{0.0 (+ n 1.0) 2e0 -0.0 1 1.5}\"` diverged from JVM.\n55\t- On JVM: explicit `cbor/float64` carriers failed `yang.clojure/compile` (`literal?`/`constant-form?`), `yin.repl` arithmetic returned bare Doubles/reboxing mismatches, `c1-3` manifest/profiles did not exist, and Gate 3 `:integral-floats` had unrecorded pins.\n56\t\n57\t---\n58\t\n59\t## 4. Shared Numeric-Token Factory Design\n60\t\n61\tImplemented in `src/cljc/yang/core/numeric_token.cljc` as the single shared numeric-token classifier and carrier constructor:\n62\t\n63\t- **Dialect table (`dialects`)**:\n64\t  - `:clojure` — supports decimal/hex/octal/`Nr` exact integers, `N`-suffixed bigints, binary64 floats (including trailing-dot `2.`, leading-`+`, exponents, symbolic `##Inf`/`##-Inf`/`##NaN`), `M`-suffixed `cbor/decimal`, and `/` `cbor/ratio` (reducing via exact GCD and refusing zero denominator). No underscore separators.\n65\t  - `:typescript` — binary64 floats (decimal/hex/binary/octal) and `n`-suffixed exact BigInts, with `_` separators.\n66\t  - `:python` — binary64 floats (including leading `.5` and trailing `2.` with `_` separators), exact integers (decimal/hex/octal/binary), and imaginary suffix classification (`:imaginary`).\n67\t  - `:php` — binary64 floats (`Real` tokens with `_` separators, leading `.5`, trailing `2.`).\n68\t- **Core API**:\n69\t  - `classify [dialect raw-text]` — pure regex/lexeme classification returning `{:kind ... :text ...}` or throwing structured `:yang.core.numeric-token/invalid-token` refusal.\n70\t  - `materialize-classified [dialect classified]` and `materialize [dialect raw-text]` — constructs canonical carriers (`cbor/float64`, `host-int/demote`, `cbor/decimal`, `cbor/ratio`) portably across JVM, Node, Dart, and Jolt (`#?(:cljd (double/parse norm) :clj (Double/parseDouble norm) :cljs (js/parseFloat norm))`).\n71\t  - `float64-token [dialect raw-text]` — direct binary64 carrier construction for float-only grammar rules.\n72\t- **Adapter migrations (zero address churn)**:\n73\t  - `src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/lower.cljc`: `number-literal` delegates to `numeric-token/classify :typescript` + `materialize-classified`; removed private `host-double`, `radix-double`, `decimal-text`.\n74\t  - `src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc`: `parse-number` delegates to `numeric-token/classify :python` + `float64-token :python`.\n75\t  - `src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc`: `float-literal` delegates to `numeric-token/float64-token :php`.\n76\t  - Added `test/yang/php/antlr/float_address_test.cljc` verifying PHP `Real` tokens (`0.0`, `1.0`, `1e0`, `2.`, `.5`, `1.5`, `1_000.0`, `9007199254740992.0`) lower to canonical `cbor/float64` distinct from `Decimal` `1` on all four hosts.\n77\t\n78\t---\n79\t\n80\t## 5. Lexical-Coverage Demonstration & Clojure Source Reader (`src/cljc/yang/clojure/reader.cljc`)\n81\t\n82\tImplemented as a self-contained, portable recursive-descent reader (zero ambient mutable state: no `*data-readers*`, no `*read-eval*`, no evaluation during reading, no global reader mutation). Every numeric token is materialized through `numeric-token/materialize :clojure` **before** any enclosing collection (`{...}`, `#{...}`) is constructed, so `{1 :a 1.0 :b}` and `#{1 1.0}` hold `1` and `Float64(1.0)` as distinct keys/members on both JVM and Node.\n83\t\n84\t| Lexical Construct | Behavior in `yang.clojure.reader` | Gate / Test Coverage |\n85\t|---|---|---|\n86\t| Whitespace & comments | Spaces, tabs, CR/LF/FF, commas, `;...` line comments, `#!...` shebang comments skipped cleanly (`\"1.0\"` inside comments never touched) | Gate 2 (`gate2-lexical-contexts-are-not-floats`) |\n87\t| Strings (`\"...\"`) | Standard escapes (`\\\"`, `\\\\`, `\\n`, `\\r`, `\\t`, `\\b`, `\\f`, `\\uXXXX`, octal `\\NNN`); numeric text inside strings remains a string | Gate 2 (`gate2-lexical-contexts-are-not-floats`) |\n88\t| Character literals (`\\...`) | Single-char, named (`\\newline`, `\\space`, `\\tab`, `\\backspace`, `\\formfeed`, `\\return`), `\\uXXXX` (surrogates refused), `\\oNNN` (range checked) | Reader unit paths & `yin.repl-test` |\n89\t| Binary64 float tokens | `0.0`, `1.0`, `-1.0`, `1e0`, `1.5`, `-0.0`, `9007199254740992.0`, `9007199254740994.0`, `1e19`, `1.5e-5`, `5e-324`, `1e-400`, `2.`, `+1.5`, `1E5` → `cbor/float64` preserving exact IEEE-754 bits | Gate 1 (`gate1-float-tokens-are-float64-content`) |\n90\t| Exact integer & bigint tokens | Plain, signed (`+7`, `-1`), hex (`0x10`), octal (`017`), radix (`2r101`, `36rZZ`), `N`-suffixed bigints (`9223372036854775808000N`) → exact integer / `big-carrier` | Gate 1 (`gate1-integer-tokens-stay-exact-integers`) |\n91\t| Decimal `M` & Ratio `/` tokens | `1M`, `10.03M`, `-2.5M` → `cbor/decimal`; `1/2` → `cbor/ratio` (reduced, zero-denominator refused) | Gate 1 (`gate1-unsupported-categories-not-relabeled`, `gate1-cross-host-canonical-identity`) |\n92\t| Symbolic values (`##`) | `##Inf`, `##-Inf`, `##NaN` → `cbor/float64` | Gate 1 / numeric-token |\n93\t| Symbols, keywords, booleans, `nil` | `true`, `false`, `nil`, `/`, qualified symbols/keywords, invalid `::` or multi-slash refused | Gate 1, Gate 2, `yin.repl-test` |\n94\t| Collections | `(...)`, `[...]`, `{...}` (even-count & duplicate-key checks), `#{...}` (duplicate-element check), `#:ns{...}` namespaced maps; `{1 :a 1.0 :b}` & `#{1 1.0}` retain both occurrences | Gate 2 (`gate2-equal-valued-occurrences-not-coalesced`), `yin.repl-test` |\n95\t| Reader macros | `'x` → `(quote x)`, `@x` → `(deref x)`, `#'x` → `(var x)`, `^:k`/`^Sym`/`^\"s\"`/`^{...}` metadata (merging onto `IObj`/`IWithMeta`), `~x`, `~@x` | Gate 2 (`gate2-lexical-contexts-are-not-floats`), `yin.repl-test` |\n96\t| Dispatch forms | `#{...}`, `#_` (parses & validates discarded form recursively, incl. nested `#_`), `#'`, `##`, `#\"...\"` regex, `#(...)` anonymous fn (nested `#()` refused), `#:ns{...}` | Gate 2, `yin.repl-test` (`regex-and-anonymous-fn-forms-read-as-on-the-jvm` now passes identically on Node too) |\n97\t| Explicit refusals | `#?` / `#?@` reader conditionals, `#=` eval, syntax-quote `` ` ``, unknown `#tag`, invalid numbers (`1.2.3`, `08`, `0x`, `1e`, `2r`), odd maps, duplicate map/set keys, unmatched/unclosed delimiters | Gate 1, Gate 2, `yin.repl-test` |\n98\t| Opt-in source positions | When `:file` or `:source-positions?` is passed in `opts` (used by `yang.io/compile-string` & `yang.io/read-source`), attaches `{:file :line :column :end-line :end-column}` via binary-searched line offsets without affecting plain `(read-forms src)` metadata | `yang.clojure-test/indexing-reader-injects-nested-source-positions` + Gate 2 metadata assertions |\n99\t\n100\t---\n101\t\n102\t## 6. Carrier Admission, Scoped Reboxing, & Entry-Point Audit\n103\t\n104\t- **`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc`**:\n105\t  - Added `numeric-carrier?` (`cbor/float64?`, `cbor/decimal?`, `cbor/ratio?`, `host-int/big-carrier?`) to `literal?` and `constant-form?`.\n106\t  - Wired `read-forms` (`[source]` / `[source opts]`) to `yang.clojure.reader/read-forms` on JVM/Node while preserving explicit `:unavailable-on-cljd` / `:unavailable-on-jolt` refusals.\n107\t  - Exported `yang.clojure/primitives` delegating to `yang.clojure.numeric/primitives`.\n108\t- **`src/cljc/yang/clojure/numeric.cljc`**:\n109\t  - Scoped carrier-aware primitives (`+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`, `=`, `==`, `!=`) backed by `yin.vm.float`, `yin.vm.integer`, and `yin.vm.data`.\n110\t  - Mixed int/float and float/float arithmetic unboxes through `yin.vm.float` and reboxes all float results as `data/float64`.\n111\t  - `=` uses kind-strict `data/equiv` (`(= 1.0 1) => false`, `(= [1.0] [1]) => false`); `==` implements Clojure's cross-kind numeric equality (`(== 1.0 1) => true`).\n112\t  - Does **not** mutate global `yin.vm/primitives` or `Float64` `:carrier-coercion` policy.\n113\t- **`src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc` & `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc`**:\n114\t  - `clojure-binding` installs `:parse yang.clojure/read-forms`, `:lower clojure-lower`, `:lower-forms clojure-lower`, `:primitives yang.clojure/primitives` on JVM/Node, and `:input :forms`, `:parse identity`, `:lower clojure-lower`, `:primitives yang.clojure/primitives` on Dart/Jolt (`:jolt` and `:cljd` ordered before `:clj` in reader conditionals!).\n115\t  - `yin.repl/compile-command-ast` uses `:lower-forms` for form-argument `(compile ...)` commands and `:parse` + `:lower` for string-argument `(compile \"...\")` commands.\n116\t  - `yin.repl/quote-symbols` renders `cbor/float64?` on `:cljs` via `DisplayKey` + `vm-float/format` (preserving `\"1.0\"`, `\"-0.0\"`, `\"##NaN\"`, `\"##Inf\"`, `\"##-Inf\"`).\n117\t- **Entry-Point & Demo Audit Ledger**:\n118\t  - `src/cljc/yang/io.cljc`: migrated `read-forms` to delegate to `yang.clojure/read-forms` with `{:file file-name}`.\n119\t  - `src/cljc/yin/repl/adapter.cljc`: audited — already forwards original source text intact; untouched.\n120\t  - `src/cljs/datomworld/demo/compilation_pipeline.cljs`: migrated from `cljs.reader` to `yang.clojure/read-forms` + `yang.clojure/primitives`.\n121\t  - `src/cljs/datomworld/demo/continuation_stream.cljs`: migrated from `cljs.reader` to `yang.clojure/read-forms` + `yang.clojure/primitives`.\n122\t  - `src/cljs/datomworld/demo/equation_plotter.cljs`: audited and explicitly documented as a legacy raw-forms host-interop boundary (binds `js/Math.*` directly and passes raw JS `Number`s to SVG geometry).\n123\t  - Shared preludes (`yang.clojure.prelude`, `yang.clojure.core-impl`, `yang.python.antlr.clj-runtime`): audited on JVM via `gate5-quoted-prelude-audit-no-integral-doubles` — **0 bare integral `Double` constants**.\n124\t\n125\t---\n126\t\n127\t## 7. Per-Gate GREEN Evidence & Four-Host Capability Matrix\n128\t\n129\t### 7.1 Four-Host Capability Classification (RULING 5 Gate 6)\n130\t\n131\t| Host | Capability Claim | Source Reading | Forms Compilation | Artifact Loading & Decode/Re-encode | Execution |\n132\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n133\t| **JVM** (`clojure 1.12.4.1602`) | `:source-text` | Verified (`yang.clojure/read-forms`, REPL, `yang.io`) | Verified (source + carrier forms + corpus) | Verified (both pre-fix `c1-2` files + embedded bytes) | Verified (AST walker, Semantic, Stack, Register VMs; linked & REPL) |\n134\t| **Node** (`node v25.6.1`, shadow-cljs) | `:source-text` | Verified (`yang.clojure/read-forms`, REPL, browser demos) | Verified (source + carrier forms + corpus) | Verified (both pre-fix `c1-2` files + embedded bytes) | Verified (AST walker, Semantic, Stac