{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_00_LgXAYTSQFWF8HC5OU6vM6972","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yang.core.numeric-token\n2\t  \"Shared numeric-token classifier and Jing carrier constructor for all Yang\n3\t   frontends (architect ruling 1795693415000, RULING 2).\n4\t\n5\t   One implementation parameterized by declarative per-language lexeme dialect\n6\t   tables (`dialects`):\n7\t   - `:clojure`    — exact integers (decimal, hex, octal, Nr..., N big-int),\n8\t                     binary64 floats (including integral floats like `0.0`,\n9\t                     `1.0`, `1e0`, `2.`, `-0.0`, and floats beyond 2^53),\n10\t                     exact decimals (`M` suffix), exact ratios (`n/d`),\n11\t                     symbolic floats (`##Inf`, `##-Inf`, `##NaN`).\n12\t   - `:python`     — underscore-separated float/int classification; float\n13\t                     tokens materialize as Jing `cbor/float64`.\n14\t   - `:php`        — underscore-separated float tokens materialize as Jing\n15\t                     `cbor/float64`.\n16\t   - `:typescript` — underscore-separated JS/TS Number tokens (decimal, hex,\n17\t                     octal, binary; refusing strict-mode legacy octal)\n18\t                     materialize as Jing `cbor/float64`.\n19\t\n20\t   No host numeric coercion guesses a lost kind: every constructor consumes\n21\t   the original lexical token string and produces canonical Jing/host Data.\"\n22\t  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n23\t            [dao.host.integer :as host-int]\n24\t            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]))\n25\t\n26\t\n27\t(def ^:private digit-alphabet \"0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz\")\n28\t\n29\t\n30\t(def dialects\n31\t  \"Declarative per-language numeric lexeme dialect table.\"\n32\t  {:clojure {:separator nil\n33\t             :kinds #{:integer :float64 :decimal :ratio :symbolic-float}\n34\t             :allow-leading-dot? false\n35\t             :allow-trailing-dot? true\n36\t             :allow-signed? true\n37\t             :allow-legacy-octal? true}\n38\t   :python {:separator \"_\"\n39\t            :kinds #{:integer :float64}\n40\t            :allow-leading-dot? true\n41\t            :allow-trailing-dot? true\n42\t            :allow-signed? false\n43\t            :allow-legacy-octal? false}\n44\t   :php {:separator \"_\"\n45\t         :kinds #{:float64}\n46\t         :allow-leading-dot? true\n47\t         :allow-trailing-dot? true\n48\t         :allow-signed? true\n49\t         :allow-legacy-octal? false}\n50\t   :typescript {:separator \"_\"\n51\t                :kinds #{:float64}\n52\t                :allow-leading-dot? true\n53\t                :allow-trailing-dot? true\n54\t                :allow-signed? false\n55\t                :allow-legacy-octal? false}})\n56\t\n57\t\n58\t(defn strip-separator\n59\t  \"Remove the dialect's digit separator (if any) from `text`.\"\n60\t  [dialect text]\n61\t  (if-let [sep (:separator (get dialects dialect))]\n62\t    (str/replace text sep \"\")\n63\t    text))\n64\t\n65\t\n66\t(defn normalize-decimal-float\n67\t  \"Normalize decimal float text (already free of digit separators) so every\n68\t   host's IEEE-754 double parser accepts it identically:\n69\t   - preserves leading `-` (including `-0.0` and `-1e-400`), strips leading `+`\n70\t   - leading `.` -> `0.`\n71\t   - `.e` / `.E` -> `.0e` / `.0E`\n72\t   - trailing `.` -> `.0`\"\n73\t  [t]\n74\t  (let [neg? (str/starts-with? t \"-\")\n75\t        pos? (str/starts-with? t \"+\")\n76\t        sign (if neg? \"-\" \"\")\n77\t        body (if (or neg? pos?) (subs t 1) t)\n78\t        body (if (str/starts-with? body \".\") (str \"0\" body) body)\n79\t        body (str/replace body \".e\" \".0e\")\n80\t        body (str/replace body \".E\" \".0E\")\n81\t        body (if (str/ends-with? body \".\") (str body \"0\") body)]\n82\t    (str sign body)))\n83\t\n84\t\n85\t(defn parse-float64\n86\t  \"Parse normalized decimal float text `t` into Jing float64 content\n87\t   (`cbor/float64`): Double on JVM, double on Dart, Float64 carrier on JS.\"\n88\t  [t]\n89\t  (let [norm (normalize-decimal-float t)\n90\t        v #?(:cljd (double/parse norm)\n91\t             :clj (Double/parseDouble norm)\n92\t             :cljs (js/parseFloat norm))]\n93\t    (cbor/float64 v)))\n94\t\n95\t\n96\t(defn parse-radix-float64\n97\t  \"Parse unsigned `digits` in `radix` (2, 8, or 16) into Jing float64 content.\"\n98\t  [digits radix]\n99\t  (let [r (double radix)\n100\t        v (reduce (fn [acc ch]\n101\t                    (+ (* acc r)\n102\t                       (double (str/index-of \"0123456789abcdef\"\n103\t                                             (str/lower-case (str ch))))))\n104\t                  0.0\n105\t                  digits)]\n106\t    (cbor/float64 v)))\n107\t\n108\t\n109\t(defn- valid-radix-digits?\n110\t  [digits radix]\n111\t  (and (pos? (count digits))\n112\t       (<= 2 radix 36)\n113\t       (let [lower (str/lower-case digits)]\n114\t         (every? (fn [ch]\n115\t                   (let [idx (str/index-of digit-alphabet (str ch))]\n116\t                     (and (some? idx) (< idx radix))))\n117\t                 lower))))\n118\t\n119\t\n120\t(defn- big-from-radix\n121\t  \"Exact non-negative host big integer from `digits` in `radix` (2..36).\"\n122\t  [digits radix]\n123\t  (let [lower (str/lower-case digits)\n124\t        r (host-int/from-native radix)]\n125\t    (reduce (fn [acc ch]\n126\t              (let [d (host-int/from-native\n127\t                        (str/index-of digit-alphabet (str ch)))]\n128\t                (host-int/add (host-int/mul acc r) d)))\n129\t            (host-int/from-native 0)\n130\t            lower)))\n131\t\n132\t\n133\t(defn- force-big-carrier\n134\t  \"Ensure host big integer `b` stays in the host's exact big-integer carrier\n135\t   (for explicit `N`-suffixed Clojure integer literals).\"\n136\t  [b]\n137\t  #?(:cljd b\n138\t     :clj (clojure.lang.BigInt/fromBigInteger b)\n139\t     :cljs b))\n140\t\n141\t\n142\t(defn parse-exact-integer\n143\t  \"Materialize exact integer content from `digits`, `radix`, `negative?`, and\n144\t   `big?` (explicit `N` suffix). Never passes through a floating intermediate.\"\n145\t  [digits radix negative? big?]\n146\t  (let [mag (if (= 10 radix)\n147\t              (host-int/parse-decimal digits)\n148\t              (big-from-radix digits radix))\n149\t        signed (if negative?\n150\t                 (host-int/sub (host-int/from-native 0) mag)\n151\t                 mag)]\n152\t    (if big?\n153\t      (force-big-carrier signed)\n154\t      (host-int/demote signed))))\n155\t\n156\t\n157\t(defn parse-decimal\n158\t  \"Parse Clojure exact decimal text `t` (without trailing `M`) into\n159\t   `cbor/decimal` without any floating intermediate.\"\n160\t  [t]\n161\t  (let [neg? (str/starts-with? t \"-\")\n162\t        pos? (str/starts-with? t \"+\")\n163\t        body (if (or neg? pos?) (subs t 1) t)\n164\t        e-idx (or (str/index-of body \"e\") (str/index-of body \"E\"))\n165\t        mant-part (if e-idx (subs body 0 e-idx) body)\n166\t        exp-part (if e-idx (subs body (inc e-idx)) nil)\n167\t        dot-idx (str/index-of mant-part \".\")\n168\t        int-digits (if dot-idx (subs mant-part 0 dot-idx) mant-part)\n169\t        frac-digits (if dot-idx (subs mant-part (inc dot-idx)) \"\")\n170\t        digits-raw (str int-digits frac-digits)\n171\t        ;; strip leading zeros so decimal-digits? gets a clean run, keeping \"0\"\n172\t        digits-trimmed (str/replace digits-raw #\"^0+\" \"\")\n173\t        digits (if (empty? digits-trimmed) \"0\" digits-trimmed)\n174\t        signed-digits (if (and neg? (not= digits \"0\")) (str \"-\" digits) digits)\n175\t        explicit-exp (if exp-part\n176\t                       (let [eneg? (str/starts-with? exp-part \"-\")\n177\t                             epos? (str/starts-with? exp-part \"+\")\n178\t                             ebody (if (or eneg? epos?) (subs exp-part 1) exp-part)\n179\t                             ebig (host-int/parse-decimal ebody)]\n180\t                         (if eneg?\n181\t                           (host-int/sub (host-int/from-native 0) ebig)\n182\t                           ebig))\n183\t                       (host-int/from-native 0))\n184\t        scale-shift (host-int/from-native (count frac-digits))\n185\t        exponent (host-int/sub explicit-exp scale-shift)\n186\t        mantissa (host-int/parse-decimal signed-digits)]\n187\t    (cbor/decimal (host-int/demote exponent) (host-int/demote mantissa))))\n188\t\n189\t\n190\t(defn parse-ratio\n191\t  \"Parse Clojure exact ratio `num-str` / `den-str`. Refuses zero denominator,\n192\t   reduces by gcd, and returns an exact integer when reduced denominator is 1\n193\t   (matching JVM Clojure's reader for e.g. `4/2` -> `2`, `0/2` -> `0`).\"\n194\t  [num-str den-str]\n195\t  (let [neg? (str/starts-with? num-str \"-\")\n196\t        pos? (str/starts-with? num-str \"+\")\n197\t        nbody (if (or neg? pos?) (subs num-str 1) num-str)\n198\t        nmag (host-int/parse-decimal nbody)\n199\t        n (if neg? (host-int/sub (host-int/from-native 0) nmag) nmag)\n200\t        d (host-int/parse-decimal den-str)\n201\t        zero (host-int/from-native 0)\n202\t        one (host-int/from-native 1)]\n203\t    (when (zero? (host-int/compare-big d zero))\n204\t      (throw (ex-info \"Divide by zero\" {:numerator num-str :denominator den-str})))\n205\t    (let [g (host-int/gcd n d)\n206\t          rn (host-int/quot-trunc n g)\n207\t          rd (host-int/quot-trunc d g)]\n208\t      (if (zero? (host-int/compare-big rd one))\n209\t        (host-int/demote rn)\n210\t        (cbor/ratio (host-int/demote rn) (host-int/demote rd))))))\n211\t\n212\t\n213\t;; =============================================================================\n214\t;; Per-dialect classifiers\n215\t;; =============================================================================\n216\t\n217\t(defn- classify-clojure\n218\t  [text]\n219\t  (cond\n220\t    (= text \"##Inf\") {:kind :symbolic-float :value ##Inf :text text}\n221\t    (= text \"##-Inf\") {:kind :symbolic-float :value ##-Inf :text text}\n222\t    (= text \"##NaN\") {:kind :symbolic-float :value ##NaN :text text}\n223\t\n224\t    ;; Decimal M literal: [+-]?[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]*)?([eE][+-]?[0-9]+)?M\n225\t    (re-matches #\"^[+-]?[0-9]+(?:\\.[0-9]*)?(?:[eE][+-]?[0-9]+)?M$\" text)\n226\t    {:kind :decimal :text (subs text 0 (dec (count text)))}\n227\t\n228\t    ;; Binary64 float literal: must contain '.' or 'e'/'E', no 'M'\n229\t    (re-matches #\"^[+-]?[0-9]+(?:\\.[0-9]*(?:[eE][+-]?[0-9]+)?|[eE][+-]?[0-9]+)$\" text)\n230\t    {:kind :float64 :text text}\n231\t\n232\t    ;; Ratio literal: [+-]?[0-9]+/[0-9]+\n233\t    (re-matches #\"^([+-]?[0-9]+)/([0-9]+)$\" text)\n234\t    (let [[_ n d] (re-matches #\"^([+-]?[0-9]+)/([0-9]+)$\" text)]\n235\t      {:kind :ratio :numerator n :denominator d :text text})\n236\t\n237\t    ;; Hex integer: [+-]?0[xX][0-9a-fA-F]+N?\n238\t    (re-matches #\"^([+-]?)0[xX]([0-9a-fA-F]+)(N?)$\" text)\n239\t    (let [[_ sign digits big-s] (re-matches #\"^([+-]?)0[xX]([0-9a-fA-F]+)(N?)$\" text)]\n240\t      {:kind :integer :radix 16 :digits digits\n241\t       :negative? (= sign \"-\") :big? (= big-s \"N\") :text text})\n242\t\n243\t    ;; Octal integer: [+-]?0[0-7]+N?\n244\t    (re-matches #\"^([+-]?)0([0-7]+)(N?)$\" text)\n245\t    (let [[_ sign digits big-s] (re-matches #\"^([+-]?)0([0-7]+)(N?)$\" text)]\n246\t      {:kind :integer :radix 8 :digits digits\n247\t       :negative? (= sign \"-\") :big? (= big-s \"N\") :text text})\n248\t\n249\t    ;; Arbitrary radix integer: [+-]?([0-9]+)[rR]([0-9a-zA-Z]+)\n250\t    (re-matches #\"^([+-]?)([0-9]+)[rR]([0-9a-zA-Z]+)$\" text)\n251\t    (let [[_ sign r-str digits] (re-matches #\"^([+-]?)([0-9]+)[rR]([0-9a-zA-Z]+)$\" text)\n252\t          radix (host-int/to-native (host-int/parse-decimal r-str))]\n253\t      (if (valid-radix-digits? digits radix)\n254\t        {:kind :integer :radix radix :digits digits\n255\t         :negative? (= sign \"-\") :big? false :text text}\n256\t        {:kind :invalid :reason :invalid-radix-number :text text}))\n257\t\n258\t    ;; Decimal integer: [+-]?(0|[1-9][0-9]*)N?\n259\t    (re-matches #\"^([+-]?)(0|[1-9][0-9]*)(N?)$\" text)\n260\t    (let [[_ sign digits big-s] (re-matches #\"^([+-]?)(0|[1-9][0-9]*)(N?)$\" text)]\n261\t      {:kind :integer :radix 10 :digits digits\n262\t       :negative? (= sign \"-\") :big? (= big-s \"N\") :text text})\n263\t\n264\t    :else\n265\t    {:kind :invalid :reason :invalid-number :text text}))\n266\t\n267\t\n268\t(defn- classify-python\n269\t  [text]\n270\t  (let [t (strip-separator :python text)\n271\t        lower (str/lower-case t)]\n272\t    (if (and (not (re-find #\"^0[xob]\" lower))\n273\t             (re-find #\"[.e]\" lower))\n274\t      {:kind :float64 :text t}\n275\t      {:kind :integer :text t})))\n276\t\n277\t\n278\t(defn- classify-php\n279\t  [text]\n280\t  {:kind :float64 :text (strip-separator :php text)})\n281\t\n282\t\n283\t(defn- classify-typescript\n284\t  [text]\n285\t  (let [t (strip-separator :typescript text)\n286\t        lower (str/lower-case t)]\n287\t    (cond\n288\t      (str/starts-with? lower \"0x\")\n289\t      (let [digits (subs lower 2)]\n290\t        (if (re-matches #\"[0-9a-f]+\" digits)\n291\t          {:kind :float64 :radix 16 :digits digits :text text}\n292\t          {:kind :invalid :reason :invalid-token :text text}))\n293\t\n294\t      (str/starts-with? lower \"0o\")\n295\t      (let [digits (subs lower 2)]\n296\t        (if (re-matches #\"[0-7]+\" digits)\n297\t          {:kind :float64 :radix 8 :digits digits :text text}\n298\t          {:kind :invalid :reason :invalid-token :text text}))\n299\t\n300\t      (str/starts-with? lower \"0b\")\n301\t      (let [digits (subs lower 2)]\n302\t        (if (re-matches #\"[01]+\" digits)\n303\t          {:kind :float64 :radix 2 :digits digits :text text}\n304\t          {:kind :invalid :reason :invalid-token :text text}))\n305\t\n306\t      (re-find #\"^0[0-9]\" lower)\n307\t      {:kind :invalid :reason :legacy-octal :text text}\n308\t\n309\t      :else\n310\t      {:kind :float64 :text t})))\n311\t\n312\t\n313\t(defn classify\n314\t  \"Classify numeric lexeme `text` under `dialect` (`:clojure`, `:python`,\n315\t   `:php`, `:typescript`). Pure and total.\"\n316\t  [dialect text]\n317\t  (case dialect\n318\t    :clojure (classify-clojure text)\n319\t    :python (classify-python text)\n320\t    :php (classify-php text)\n321\t    :typescript (classify-typescript text)\n322\t    {:kind :invalid :reason :unknown-dialect :dialect dialect :text text}))\n323\t\n324\t\n325\t(defn materialize-classified\n326\t  \"Construct canonical Jing/host Data from a `classify` result map. Throws\n327\t   on `:invalid`.\"\n328\t  [{:keys [kind text radix digits negative? big? numerator denominator value]\n329\t    :as classified}]\n330\t  (case kind\n331\t    :float64 (if radix\n332\t               (parse-radix-float64 digits radix)\n333\t               (parse-float64 text))\n334\t    :symbolic-float (cbor/float64 value)\n335\t    :integer (parse-exact-integer digits radix negative? big?)\n336\t    :decimal (parse-decimal text)\n337\t    :ratio (parse-ratio numerator denominator)\n338\t    (throw (ex-info (str \"Invalid number: \" text)\n339\t                    (assoc classified :type :reader-exception :ex-kind :reader-error)))))\n340\t\n341\t\n342\t(defn materialize\n343\t  \"Classify and materialize numeric token `text` under `dialect` into\n344\t   canonical Jing/host Data.\"\n345\t  [dialect text]\n346\t  (materialize-classified (classify dialect text)))\n347\t\n348\t\n349\t(defn float64-token\n350\t  \"Materialize a lexeme already known by `dialect`'s grammar to be a\n351\t   floating-point literal into Jing float64 content.\"\n352\t  [dialect text]\n353\t  (parse-float64 (strip-separator dialect text)))\n354\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f2c1e4a-7b3d-4e8f-a6c5-d0e9f8a1b2c3","uuid":"7484c482-1752-4186-946b-24a44c2b63da","timestamp":"2026-11-26T15:26:29.441Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/sto/ci/datomworld-floatkind/src/cljc/yang/core/numeric_token.cljc","content":"(ns yang.core.numeric-token\n  \"Shared numeric-token classifier and Jing carrier constructor for all Yang\n   frontends (architect ruling 1795693415000, RULING 2).\n\n   One implementation parameterized by declarative per-language lexeme dialect\n   tables (`dialects`):\n   - `:clojure`    — exact integers (decimal, hex, octal, Nr..., N big-int),\n                     binary64 floats (including integral floats like `0.0`,\n                     `1.0`, `1e0`, `2.`, `-0.0`, and floats beyond 2^53),\n                     exact decimals (`M` suffix), exact ratios (`n/d`),\n                     symbolic floats (`##Inf`, `##-Inf`, `##NaN`).\n   - `:python`     — underscore-separated float/int classification; float\n                     tokens materialize as Jing `cbor/float64`.\n   - `:php`        — underscore-separated float tokens materialize as Jing\n                     `cbor/float64`.\n   - `:typescript` — underscore-separated JS/TS Number tokens (decimal, hex,\n                     octal, binary; refusing strict-mode legacy octal)\n                     materialize as Jing `cbor/float64`.\n\n   No host numeric coercion guesses a lost kind: every constructor consumes\n   the original lexical token string and produces canonical Jing/host Data.\"\n  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n            [dao.host.integer :as host-int]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]))\n\n\n(def ^:private digit-alphabet \"0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz\")\n\n\n(def dialects\n  \"Declarative per-language numeric lexeme dialect table.\"\n  {:clojure {:separator nil\n             :kinds #{:integer :float64 :decimal :ratio :symbolic-float}\n             :allow-leading-dot? false\n             :allow-trailing-dot? true\n             :allow-signed? true\n             :allow-legacy-octal? true}\n   :python {:separator \"_\"\n            :kinds #{:integer :float64}\n            :allow-leading-dot? true\n            :allow-trailing-dot? true\n            :allow-signed? false\n            :allow-legacy-octal? false}\n   :php {:separator \"_\"\n         :kinds #{:float64}\n         :allow-leading-dot? true\n         :allow-trailing-dot? true\n         :allow-signed? true\n         :allow-legacy-octal? false}\n   :typescript {:separator \"_\"\n                :kinds #{:float64}\n                :allow-leading-dot? true\n                :allow-trailing-dot? true\n                :allow-signed? false\n                :allow-legacy-octal? false}})\n\n\n(defn strip-separator\n  \"Remove the dialect's digit separator (if any) from `text`.\"\n  [dialect text]\n  (if-let [sep (:separator (get dialects dialect))]\n    (str/replace text sep \"\")\n    text))\n\n\n(defn normalize-decimal-float\n  \"Normalize decimal float text (already free of digit separators) so every\n   host's IEEE-754 double parser accepts it identically:\n   - preserves leading `-` (including `-0.0` and `-1e-400`), strips leading `+`\n   - leading `.` -> `0.`\n   - `.e` / `.E` -> `.0e` / `.0E`\n   - trailing `.` -> `.0`\"\n  [t]\n  (let [neg? (str/starts-with? t \"-\")\n        pos? (str/starts-with? t \"+\")\n        sign (if neg? \"-\" \"\")\n        body (if (or neg? pos?) (subs t 1) t)\n        body (if (str/starts-with? body \".\") (str \"0\" body) body)\n        body (str/replace body \".e\" \".0e\")\n        body (str/replace body \".E\" \".0E\")\n        body (if (str/ends-with? body \".\") (str body \"0\") body)]\n    (str sign body)))\n\n\n(defn parse-float64\n  \"Parse normalized decimal float text `t` into Jing float64 content\n   (`cbor/float64`): Double on JVM, double on Dart, Float64 carrier on JS.\"\n  [t]\n  (let [norm (normalize-decimal-float t)\n        v #?(:cljd (double/parse norm)\n             :clj (Double/parseDouble norm)\n             :cljs (js/parseFloat norm))]\n    (cbor/float64 v)))\n\n\n(defn parse-radix-float64\n  \"Parse unsigned `digits` in `radix` (2, 8, or 16) into Jing float64 content.\"\n  [digits radix]\n  (let [r (double radix)\n        v (reduce (fn [acc ch]\n                    (+ (* acc r)\n                       (double (str/index-of \"0123456789abcdef\"\n                                             (str/lower-case (str ch))))))\n                  0.0\n                  digits)]\n    (cbor/float64 v)))\n\n\n(defn- valid-radix-digits?\n  [digits radix]\n  (and (pos? (count digits))\n       (<= 2 radix 36)\n       (let [lower (str/lower-case digits)]\n         (every? (fn [ch]\n                   (let [idx (str/index-of digit-alphabet (str ch))]\n                     (and (some? idx) (< idx radix))))\n                 lower))))\n\n\n(defn- big-from-radix\n  \"Exact non-negative host big integer from `digits` in `radix` (2..36).\"\n  [digits radix]\n  (let [lower (str/lower-case digits)\n        r (host-int/from-native radix)]\n    (reduce (fn [acc ch]\n              (let [d (host-int/from-native\n                        (str/index-of digit-alphabet (str ch)))]\n                (host-int/add (host-int/mul acc r) d)))\n            (host-int/from-native 0)\n            lower)))\n\n\n(defn- force-big-carrier\n  \"Ensure host big integer `b` stays in the host's exact big-integer carrier\n   (for explicit `N`-suffixed Clojure integer literals).\"\n  [b]\n  #?(:cljd b\n     :clj (clojure.lang.BigInt/fromBigInteger b)\n     :cljs b))\n\n\n(defn parse-exact-integer\n  \"Materialize exact integer content from `digits`, `radix`, `negative?`, and\n   `big?` (explicit `N` suffix). Never passes through a floating intermediate.\"\n  [digits radix negative? big?]\n  (let [mag (if (= 10 radix)\n              (host-int/parse-decimal digits)\n              (big-from-radix digits radix))\n        signed (if negative?\n                 (host-int/sub (host-int/from-native 0) mag)\n                 mag)]\n    (if big?\n      (force-big-carrier signed)\n      (host-int/demote signed))))\n\n\n(defn parse-decimal\n  \"Parse Clojure exact decimal text `t` (without trailing `M`) into\n   `cbor/decimal` without any floating intermediate.\"\n  [t]\n  (let [neg? (str/starts-with? t \"-\")\n        pos? (str/starts-with? t \"+\")\n        body (if (or neg? pos?) (subs t 1) t)\n        e-idx (or (str/index-of body \"e\") (str/index-of body \"E\"))\n        mant-part (if e-idx (subs body 0 e-idx) body)\n        exp-part (if e-idx (subs body (inc e-idx)) nil)\n        dot-idx (str/index-of mant-part \".\")\n        int-digits (if dot-idx (subs mant-part 0 dot-idx) mant-part)\n        frac-digits (if dot-idx (subs mant-part (inc dot-idx)) \"\")\n        digits-raw (str int-digits frac-digits)\n        ;; strip leading zeros so decimal-digits? gets a clean run, keeping \"0\"\n        digits-trimmed (str/replace digits-raw #\"^0+\" \"\")\n        digits (if (empty? digits-trimmed) \"0\" digits-trimmed)\n        signed-digits (if (and neg? (not= digits \"0\")) (str \"-\" digits) digits)\n        explicit-exp (if exp-part\n                       (let [eneg? (str/starts-with? exp-part \"-\")\n                             epos? (str/starts-with? exp-part \"+\")\n                             ebody (if (or eneg? epos?) (subs exp-part 1) exp-part)\n                             ebig (host-int/parse-decimal ebody)]\n                         (if eneg?\n                           (host-int/sub (host-int/from-native 0) ebig)\n                           ebig))\n                       (host-int/from-native 0))\n        scale-shift (host-int/from-native (count frac-digits))\n        exponent (host-int/sub explicit-exp scale-shift)\n        mantissa (host-int/parse-decimal signed-digits)]\n    (cbor/decimal (host-int/demote exponent) (host-int/demote mantissa))))\n\n\n(defn parse-ratio\n  \"Parse Clojure exact ratio `num-str` / `den-str`. Refuses zero denominator,\n   reduces by gcd, and returns an exact integer when reduced denominator is 1\n   (matching JVM Clojure's reader for e.g. `4/2` -> `2`, `0/2` -> `0`).\"\n  [num-str den-str]\n  (let [neg? (str/starts-with? num-str \"-\")\n        pos? (str/starts-with? num-str \"+\")\n        nbody (if (or neg? pos?) (subs num-str 1) num-str)\n        nmag (host-int/parse-decimal nbody)\n        n (if neg? (host-int/sub (host-int/from-native 0) nmag) nmag)\n        d (host-int/parse-decimal den-str)\n        zero (host-int/from-native 0)\n        one (host-int/from-native 1)]\n    (when (zero? (host-int/compare-big d zero))\n      (throw (ex-info \"Divide by zero\" {:numerator num-str :denominator den-str})))\n    (let [g (host-int/gcd n d)\n          rn (host-int/quot-trunc n g)\n          rd (host-int/quot-trunc d g)]\n      (if (zero? (host-int/compare-big rd one))\n        (host-int/demote rn)\n        (cbor/ratio (host-int/demote rn) (host-int/demote rd))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Per-dialect classifiers\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- classify-clojure\n  [text]\n  (cond\n    (= text \"##Inf\") {:kind :symbolic-float :value ##Inf :text text}\n    (= text \"##-Inf\") {:kind :symbolic-float :value ##-Inf :text text}\n    (= text \"##NaN\") {:kind :symbolic-float :value ##NaN :text text}\n\n    ;; Decimal M literal: [+-]?[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]*)?([eE][+-]?[0-9]+)?M\n    (re-matches #\"^[+-]?[0-9]+(?:\\.[0-9]*)?(?:[eE][+-]?[0-9]+)?M$\" text)\n    {:kind :decimal :text (subs text 0 (dec (count text)))}\n\n    ;; Binary64 float literal: must contain '.' or 'e'/'E', no 'M'\n    (re-matches #\"^[+-]?[0-9]+(?:\\.[0-9]*(?:[eE][+-]?[0-9]+)?|[eE][+-]?[0-9]+)$\" text)\n    {:kind :float64 :text text}\n\n    ;; Ratio literal: [+-]?[0-9]+/[0-9]+\n    (re-matches #\"^([+-]?[0-9]+)/([0-9]+)$\" text)\n    (let [[_ n d] (re-matches #\"^([+-]?[0-9]+)/([0-9]+)$\" text)]\n      {:kind :ratio :numerator n :denominator d :text text})\n\n    ;; Hex integer: [+-]?0[xX][0-9a-fA-F]+N?\n    (re-matches #\"^([+-]?)0[xX]([0-9a-fA-F]+)(N?)$\" text)\n    (let [[_ sign digits big-s] (re-matches #\"^([+-]?)0[xX]([0-9a-fA-F]+)(N?)$\" text)]\n      {:kind :integer :radix 16 :digits digits\n       :negative? (= sign \"-\") :big? (= big-s \"N\") :text text})\n\n    ;; Octal integer: [+-]?0[0-7]+N?\n    (re-matches #\"^([+-]?)0([0-7]+)(N?)$\" text)\n    (let [[_ sign digits big-s] (re-matches #\"^([+-]?)0([0-7]+)(N?)$\" text)]\n      {:kind :integer :radix 8 :digits digits\n       :negative? (= sign \"-\") :big? (= big-s \"N\") :text text})\n\n    ;; Arbitrary radix integer: [+-]?([0-9]+)[rR]([0-9a-zA-Z]+)\n    (re-matches #\"^([+-]?)([0-9]+)[rR]([0-9a-zA-Z]+)$\" text)\n    (let [[_ sign r-str digits] (re-matches #\"^([+-]?)([0-9]+)[rR]([0-9a-zA-Z]+)$\" text)\n          radix (host-int/to-native (host-int/parse-decimal r-str))]\n      (if (valid-radix-digits? digits radix)\n        {:kind :integer :radix radix :digits digits\n         :negative? (= sign \"-\") :big? false :text text}\n        {:kind :invalid :reason :invalid-radix-number :text text}))\n\n    ;; Decimal integer: [+-]?(0|[1-9][0-9]*)N?\n    (re-matches #\"^([+-]?)(0|[1-9][0-9]*)(N?)$\" text)\n    (let [[_ sign digits big-s] (re-matches #\"^([+-]?)(0|[1-9][0-9]*)(N?)$\" text)]\n      {:kind :integer :radix 10 :digits digits\n       :negative? (= sign \"-\") :big? (= big-s \"N\") :text text})\n\n    :else\n    {:kind :invalid :reason :invalid-number :text text}))\n\n\n(defn- classify-python\n  [text]\n  (let [t (strip-separator :python text)\n        lower (str/lower-case t)]\n    (if (and (not (re-find #\"^0[xob]\" lower))\n             (re-find #\"[.e]\" lower))\n      {:kind :float64 :text t}\n      {:kind :integer :text t})))\n\n\n(defn- classify-php\n  [text]\n  {:kind :float64 :text (strip-separator :php text)})\n\n\n(defn- classify-typescript\n  [text]\n  (let [t (strip-separator :typescript text)\n        lower (str/lower-case t)]\n    (cond\n      (str/starts-with? lower \"0x\")\n      (let [digits (subs lower 2)]\n        (if (re-matches #\"[0-9a-f]+\" digits)\n          {:kind :float64 :radix 16 :digits digits :text text}\n          {:kind :invalid :reason :invalid-token :text text}))\n\n      (str/starts-with? lower \"0o\")\n      (let [digits (subs lower 2)]\n        (if (re-matches #\"[0-7]+\" digits)\n          {:kind :float64 :radix 8 :digits digits :text text}\n          {:kind :invalid :reason :invalid-token :text text}))\n\n      (str/starts-with? lower \"0b\")\n      (let [digits (subs lower 2)]\n        (if (re-matches #\"[01]+\" digits)\n          {:kind :float64 :radix 2 :digits digits :text text}\n          {:kind :invalid :reason :invalid-token :text text}))\n\n      (re-find #\"^0[0-9]\" lower)\n      {:kind :invalid :reason :legacy-octal :text text}\n\n      :else\n      {:kind :float64 :text t})))\n\n\n(defn classify\n  \"Classify numeric lexeme `text` under `dialect` (`:clojure`, `:python`,\n   `:php`, `:typescript`). Pure and total.\"\n  [dialect text]\n  (case dialect\n    :clojure (classify-clojure text)\n    :python (classify-python text)\n    :php (classify-php text)\n    :typescript (classify-typescript text)\n    {:kind :invalid :reason :unknown-dialect :dialect dialect :text text}))\n\n\n(defn materialize-classified\n  \"Construct canonical Jing/host Data from a `classify` result map. Throws\n   on `:invalid`.\"\n  [{:keys [kind text radix digits negative? big? numerator denominator value]\n    :as classified}]\n  (case kind\n    :float64 (if radix\n               (parse-radix-float64 digits radix)\n               (parse-float64 text))\n    :symbolic-float (cbor/float64 value)\n    :integer (parse-exact-integer digits radix negative? big?)\n    :decimal (parse-decimal text)\n    :ratio (parse-ratio numerator denominator)\n    (throw (ex-info (str \"Invalid number: \" text)\n                    (assoc classified :type :reader-exception :ex-kind :reader-error)))))\n\n\n(defn materialize\n  \"Classify and materialize numeric token `text` under `dialect` into\n   canonical Jing/host Data.\"\n  [dialect text]\n  (materialize-classified (classify dialect text)))\n\n\n(defn float64-token\n  \"Materialize a lexeme already known by `dialect`'s grammar to be a\n   floating-point literal into Jing float64 content.\"\n  [dialect text]\n  (parse-float64 (strip-separator dialect text)))\n","numLines":354,"startLine":1,"totalLines":354}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_00_LgXAYTSQFWF8HC5OU6vM6972","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
