{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"98fd6f98-910d-4de8-a9d1-76d46096a686","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. The test uses `data/float-value` and IEEE bit comparisons, `data-equiv`, etc. This is substantive. The float tokens include `5e-324` (min subnormal), `1e-400` (underflow to zero), `+1.5`, `2.`, `1E5`.\n\nNote: the `host-bits-of` on cljs constructs the bits via DataView big-endian (setFloat64 with littleEndian=false → big-endian) then reads bytes 0..7 and formats. So it's big-endian hex. On JVM `Double/doubleToLongBits` gives a long whose hex is big-endian order matching the double bit pattern. So both produce big-endian hex. Good, cross-host consistent.\n\nNow let me read gates 2-7 substance. Let me read 186-392 and 393-820.","signature":"98fd6f98-910d-4de8-a9d1-76d46096a686"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2026,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":78336,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f2c1e4a-7b3d-4e8f-a6c5-d0e9f8a1b2c3","uuid":"4dac847f-9f7f-424a-a0f3-e14f0f6a700a","timestamp":"2026-11-26T15:29:01.751Z","thinking_duration_ms":3862,"thinking_display":"updates"}
