{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"60c06353-18f5-472e-913f-39044979bd40","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent. The tests are substantive. The gate4-unboxed-control is the mutation control: on JS, unboxed `1.0` compiles as integer (the defect), boxed source path compiles as float, and digests differ. On JVM both are float. This matches the ruling's \"dropping boxing fails both oracle and digest\".\n\nLet me read the rest (gate 6, gate 7, and the end).","signature":"60c06353-18f5-472e-913f-39044979bd40"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3300,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":82560,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f2c1e4a-7b3d-4e8f-a6c5-d0e9f8a1b2c3","uuid":"90fb7abf-c0e2-49dd-8899-88aef6881bb8","timestamp":"2026-11-26T15:29:08.176Z","thinking_duration_ms":2104,"thinking_display":"updates"}
