ad NO `:primitives` key. So `(:primitives (:binding selected))` would be nil, and `(merge vm/primitives nil)` = vm/primitives (raw host primitives). So the test would still run but fail at the arithmetic checks (bare Number results).\n\nWait, but the red-node run shows 75 failures 5 errors, and the errors would be from things like `yang.clojure/primitives` not existing... Actually the test ns requires `[yin.repl.frontends :as frontends]` and uses `frontends/standard`, `frontend/select`. These exist pre-fix.\n\nActually, let me not over-analyze. The red logs exist with genuine content. The key question is whether the tests were RUNNABLE pre-fix (i.e., the test file compiled against pre-fix source). The red logs prove they ran and failed. The errors (5 on node) would include e.g. `gate5-explicit-carrier-forms-compile-and-run` failing because `yang/compile` refused carriers (the carrier-admission gap) — that's an ERROR not a FAIL? Or the `numeric-token` ns not existing → but the test doesn't reference numeric-token directly.\n\nLet me check what the 5 errors on Node were. Actually, let me check the red-node errors quickly.","signature":"a1ed0ed8-b0f6-4e47-a913-b543250a1b1c"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":494,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":109824,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f2c1e4a-7b3d-4e8f-a6c5-d0e9f8a1b2c3","uuid":"ee25e9b2-0712-4620-9a56-fe3ea1b893c9","timestamp":"2026-11-26T15:30:31.523Z","thinking_duration_ms":18948,"thinking_display":"updates"}
