{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_00_llhTJDuMmfdtpKLXmEOr3058","type":"tool_result","content":"diff --git a/docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md b/docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md\nindex d9575be7..5a14c291 100644\n--- a/docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md\n+++ b/docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md\n@@ -391,7 +391,9 @@ three cases are independent of argument order and of which host runs them:\n   JavaScript returns the carrier so re-encoding cannot lose its kind.\n   Carrying float kind is the producer's obligation; the codec never infers\n   it. The Python frontend's ruling on meeting it is `yang.antlr.md`\n-  section 8.5.5.\n+  section 8.5.5, and the Clojure source/forms producer contract and\n+  shared numeric-token factory (`yang.core.numeric-token`) are specified\n+  in `yang.antlr.md` section 8.8.\n - The JavaScript float64 carrier refuses numeric and default coercion: its\n   `valueOf` throws the refusal `:carrier-coercion` (raised through the\n   codec's refusal helper, so `refusal` reads it; it is not a corpus\ndiff --git a/docs/design/yang.preludes.md b/docs/design/yang.preludes.md\nindex 268614ae..8fd346df 100644\n--- a/docs/design/yang.preludes.md\n+++ b/docs/design/yang.preludes.md\n@@ -609,7 +609,7 @@ def sum_even_squares(xs):\n ### 8.1 Multi-host portability (JVM, CLJS/Node, CLJD/Dart, Jolt/Scheme)\n \n - **ClojureDart AOT literal limits:** Consolidate `defquoted` into **`yang.core.defquoted`** (r8 M9 — the dedicated host macro namespace; NOT `yang.core.prelude`, keeping the emission namespace free of macro definitions).\n-- **Zero bare integral float literals & zero raw host doubles in guest UAST:** All float operations pass boxed `data/float64` through `yin.vm.float`, avoiding raw host doubles across JVM, Node, Dart, and Jolt.\n+- **Zero bare integral float literals & zero raw host doubles in guest UAST:** All float operations pass boxed `data/float64` through `yin.vm.float`, avoiding raw host doubles across JVM, Node, Dart, and Jolt. Shared prelude and runtime emitters (`yang.clojure.prelude`, `yang.clojure.core-impl`, `yang.python.antlr.clj-runtime`, and Track B language preludes) must never embed bare integral `Double` constants in host-quoted tables (audited on the JVM); every float literal is constructed explicitly as `dao.jing.cbor/float64` (via `yang.core.numeric-token` at frontend token time per [`docs/design/yang.antlr.md` §8.8](./yang.antlr.md#88-the-producer-owns-float-kind)) and float-returning primitives rebox their results via `yin.vm.float` before returning to VM execution or collection key positions.\n - **Canonical ordering (`b86bc0e8` invariant):** Recipes, profiles, descriptor maps, and emitted UAST operand sequences sort keys deterministically, guaranteeing byte-identical `dao.jing.cbor` hashes across all 4 hosts.\n - **No JVM-only reflection:** `yang.core.semantics` and `yang.core.prelude` use pure portable Clojure data transforms.\n \ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yang/docs/yang_implementation.md b/src/cljc/yang/docs/yang_implementation.md\nindex d04f17e1..04c1f582 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yang/docs/yang_implementation.md\n+++ b/src/cljc/yang/docs/yang_implementation.md\n@@ -228,9 +228,16 @@ The Yang compiler is **fully functional** and **production-ready** for compiling\n \n The compiler demonstrates the power of the Yin/Yang dual system: **Yang generates continuations, Yin executes them**. Together they enable code to become data, data to become computation, and computation to migrate freely across platforms.\n \n+## Portability and Numeric-Kind Contract\n+\n+`yin.vm` on JVM, Node (JS), Dart, and Jolt preserves the numeric kind carried by portable Data and canonically encoded Jing artifacts (`dao.jing.cbor.md`), subject to the selected runtime/profile's supported operations:\n+\n+- **Source-text compilation (`:yang/clojure` revision `c1-3`, `:source-text` capability on JVM and Node):** `yang.clojure/read-forms` (via `yang.clojure.reader` and the shared `yang.core.numeric-token` factory) preserves binary64 floating-point kind (including integral-valued floats such as `0.0`, `1.0`, `1e0`, `-0.0`, and floats at/beyond `2^53`), exact integers/bigints, decimals (`M`), and ratios before collection construction or lowering. The standard REPL/catalog route (`yin.repl.frontends/standard`) routes source text directly through `yang.clojure/read-forms` and installs scoped carrier-aware numeric primitives (`yang.clojure/primitives`) that rebox floating results.\n+- **Forms-only boundary (all hosts, and `:forms-only` capability on Dart and Jolt):** `yang.clojure/compile` and `compile-program` admit Jing numeric carriers (`dao.jing.cbor/float64`, `decimal`, `ratio`, and exact big-integer carriers) directly, nested, and quoted. On JavaScript, a bare integral JS `Number` denotes exact integer content; callers intending floating Data through the forms API must supply `dao.jing.cbor/float64` / `yin.vm.data/float64`. See `docs/design/yang.antlr.md` §8.8 for the full contract, revision `c1-3` profiles, legacy custody rules, and four-host capability matrix.\n+\n ---\n \n-**Implementation Date**: 2025-11-13\n+**Implementation Date**: 2025-11-13 (numeric-kind portability revision `c1-3` documented 2026-11-26)\n **Total Lines of Code**: ~600 (compiler + tests + docs)\n **Test Coverage**: 100% of implemented features\n **Platforms**: JVM, Node.js (browser-ready)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f2c1e4a-7b3d-4e8f-a6c5-d0e9f8a1b2c3","uuid":"9e503504-82a8-4456-93b8-e833cc8263b7","timestamp":"2026-11-26T15:30:51.229Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"diff --git a/docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md b/docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md\nindex d9575be7..5a14c291 100644\n--- a/docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md\n+++ b/docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md\n@@ -391,7 +391,9 @@ three cases are independent of argument order and of which host runs them:\n   JavaScript returns the carrier so re-encoding cannot lose its kind.\n   Carrying float kind is the producer's obligation; the code