h a disposition note, but it doesn't change the verdict because the underlying fixes are verified green in a later log.\n\nWait, let me also double-check: are the 3 indexing failures actually FIXED by the current code (not just the test skipped)? The green-jvm-repl-clojure.log (10:06) shows yang.clojure-test + yin.repl-test with 0 failures, 0 errors — 157 tests. So `indexing-reader-injects-nested-source-positions` passes. Good.\n\nBut hold on — is there a possibility that the green-jvm-repl-clojure.log run did NOT include `indexing-reader-injects-nested-source-positions` because of a namespace filter? No — it ran `yang.clojure-test` fully (157 tests total includes all its tests). And 0 failures. So the indexing test passes now.\n\nNow, one more thing to verify for honesty: the findings say \"yang.clojure-test + yin.repl-test: 157 tests, 1,264 assertions, 0 failures\". green-jvm-repl-clojure.log confirms \"157 tests, 1264 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors\". ✓.\n\nAnd the regressions: the findings say \"10 other namespaces: 154 tests, 2,395 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors\". The log shows the full run (311 tests) with the 7 failures in the 2 non-oracle namespaces. The 10 oracle namespaces = 311 - 157 = 154 tests, and their assertions = 3659 - 1264 = 2395. And 0 of the 7 failures were in those 10 namespaces (they were all in yang.clojure-test and yin.repl-test). So the \"154/2395/0\" claim is accurate for the oracle subset, but the cited log file overall shows 7 failures.\n\nOK. This is a finding about evidence hygiene. Let me note it, but it's minor.\n\nLet me now check the Node regression log to see if it's similarly contaminated.","signature":"7e44db5a-5ac5-44fa-8313-930d68c3da32"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1140,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":134016,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f2c1e4a-7b3d-4e8f-a6c5-d0e9f8a1b2c3","uu