{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"2efb270b-2af8-4bbb-b8ec-d0b6a6c23f5c","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The write needs permission. Let me retry — actually, the permission was not granted yet; I should wait. The tool result says \"you haven't granted it yet\". This means the user needs to grant it. But I should just retry? No — the instruction says a denied call means the user declined. But this says \"you haven't granted it yet\" — it's a pending permission prompt, not a denial.\n\nActually, in this harness, when a Write requires permission and it's not granted, it returns this message. I should perhaps retry once, or wait. Actually, the message indicates the permission is pending/not granted. Let me just retry the write — but that might re-prompt. \n\nHmm, actually, re-reading: \"Claude requested permissions to write ... but you haven't granted it yet.\" This is the permission system telling me the write is awaiting approval. The appropriate action is to wait for the user to grant. But I can't \"wait\" — I should perhaps retry the write call. In practice, retrying the same call after a permission denial is discouraged (\"a denied call means the user declined it — adjust, don't retry verbatim\"). But this isn't a denial; it's \"haven't granted yet\".\n\nLet me just retry the Write once. Actually, the safest is to retry — the user may grant on retry. Let me retry the write.","signature":"2efb270b-2af8-4bbb-b8ec-d0b6a6c23f5c"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":137,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":152576,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f2c1e4a-7b3d-4e8f-a6c5-d0e9f8a1b2c3","uuid":"7afac45f-6d7f-4b77-aca7-24b03bc42a61","timestamp":"2026-11-26T15:37:07.603Z","thinking_duration_ms":4183,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"2efb270b-2af8-4bbb-b8ec-d0b6a6c23f5c","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_00_qfDLwn30t9eXnEdurVM92433","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/sto/ci/datomworld-floatkind/collab/yang-clojure/1795706698000-reviewer-float-kind-r1.deepseek-v4-pro.findings.md","content":"Created-GMT: 2026-11-26 15:36:27 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-26 10:36:27 EST\nRole: Reviewer (numeric semantics + compiler provenance)\nCoding-Agent: deepseek (deepseek-v4-pro)\nAuthor-under-review: gemini-4-neon (findings `1795706286000-engineer-float-kind-portability-r1.gemini-4-neon.findings.md`)\nInspected HEAD: `42b8cfc6` (merge of fix `3b850212` and docs `8214a3ed`)\n\n# Verdict: APPROVE (with one non-blocking evidence-hygiene disposition)\n\nI verified the work against sources and logs, not the author's prose. All six\nreview obligations pass; the implementation conforms to ruling `1795693415000`\n(RULING 1–5) and the round brief. One evidence-log hygiene issue is below\n(D-1); it does not change the verdict because the underlying code and the\nclean re-verification both exist.\n\n## 1. TDD authenticity — CONFIRMED\n\nRED logs (`collab/yang-clojure/1795702210000-floatkind-evidence/`, 09:12–09:24)\nare genuine pre-implementation failures on the unfixed code paths:\n\n- `red-node-gates1245.log`: `0.0→0`, `1.0→1`, `-1.0→-1`, `1e0→1`,\n  `9007199254740992.0→9007199254740992`, `1e19→10000000000000000000`,\n  `2.→2`, `1E5→100000`; `1e-400` underflows to integer `0`;\n  `9223372036854775808000N→9.223372036854776e+21` (float!); `1/2→0.5`;\n  `1M→1`; `10.03M→10.03`. These are exactly the pre-fix `cljs.tools.reader`\n  kind-loss modes the ruling documented. Summary `17 tests / 163 assertions /\n  63 failures, 4 errors` matches the findings.\n- `red-jvm-gates1245.log`: `18 tests / 180 assertions / 20 failures, 1 error`,\n  failing on unrecorded reference pins + missing `c1-3` manifest/profile and\n  the carrier-admission gap. Matches.\n- `red-node-all7gates.log`: `22 tests / 214 assertions / 75 failures, 5 errors`\n  (the 5 errors are the documented carrier-admission/coalescing/corpus paths);\n  `red-jvm-all7gates.log` gate-3 sub-run `2 tests / 22 assertions / 2 failures`\n  on the unrecorded `:integral-floats` pin. Matches.\n\nGREEN logs (09:49–10:17) show 0 failures/errors and the exact claimed counts\n(JVM 22/290, JVM corpus 2/22, Node 24/310, JVM repl+clojure 157/1264, Node\nregressions 178/2137, Dart 63/63, Jolt 55/55 float-kind + 45 PHP + 108 float).\n\n## 2. RULING 2 conformance — CONFIRMED\n\n`src/cljc/yang/clojure/reader.cljc` is a self-contained recursive-descent\nreader. Numeric tokens are materialized through `numeric-token/materialize\n:clojure` **at token time** (lines 520, 653–654), before `build-checked-map` /\n`build-checked-set` / any lowering can coalesce `1` and `1.0`. Verified:\nno regex-over-source (token classification regex is the ANTLR producer\nprecedent, not textual source substitution), no postwalk over read Numbers,\nno print-round-trip, no `*data-readers*`/`*read-eval*`/global reader mutation.\nLexical coverage is demonstrated in the namespace docstring and exercised by\nGate 2 (`comments/strings/chars/quote/metadata/dispatch/conditionals/discard`),\nall green on JVM+Node. Refusals are explicit (`#?`, `#?@`, `#=`, syntax-quote,\nunknown `#tag`, malformed numbers/collections).\n\n## 3. RULING 5 scope — CONFIRMED\n\nAll changed files are inside the boundaries. One shared factory\n`src/cljc/yang/core/numeric_token.cljc`; the four frontends route through it\n(Clojure reader `:clojure` dialect; TS/Python/PHP lowerers delegate — no fourth\nprivate copy). The TS/Python/PHP diffs are behavior-preserving (I diffed the\nold `host-double`/`radix-double`/`decimal-text` and Python `parse-number`/PHP\n`float-literal` against the new `classify`/`materialize` paths: same token\nclassification, same double parse after identical normalization; the Python\n`j`-imaginary refusal and TS legacy-octal/strict-hex refusal are retained).\n`yang/io.cljc` is a minimal source-entry migration (read-forms → token-aware\nreader with `:file` positions), covered by the \"integrate actual source entry\npaths\" clause. Demos migrated (`compilation_pipeline`, `continuation_stream`)\nor explicitly delimited as legacy raw-forms (`equation_plotter`), per RULING 5.\n\n## 4. Gates 1–7 substance — CONFIRMED\n\n- Gate 1: real identical source strings through the frontend source entry and\n  the REPL/catalog route, with IEEE-bit comparisons (`host-bits-of`) and integer\n  controls, `M`/ratio/`N` categories not relabeled, invalid tokens refused.\n- Gate 2: top-level/binding/vector/quoted/nested/map/set/call-argument\n  positions; `{1 :a 1.0 :b}` and `#{1 1.0}` keep both occurrences on JVM and\n  Node; comments/strings/discard controls; macro-generated float; float-key\n  refusal parity (`:coll/unsupported-key`).\n- Gate 3: `:integral-floats` restored to the common corpus (19 cases) with ONE\n  recorded reference, plus `unmodified-source-integral-floats-test` comparing\n  `\"{0.0 (+ n 1.0) 2e0 -0.0 1 1.5}\"` against that same reference (not\n  per-host-regenerated), with an integer control asserted distinct.\n- Gate 4: kind-strict oracle (`equiv`, nested, `admit-key?`, `content=` vs\n  `equiv` for `±0.0` and NaN), `inc`/`dec` float vs integer branch, REPL\n  arithmetic reboxing, and the mutation control `gate4-unboxed-control`\n  (on JS `compile 1.0` is integer content and the digest differs from the\n  source path; on JVM both are float — dropping boxing fails both oracle and\n  digest). Linked/library path exercised separately.\n- Gate 5: explicit carrier forms compile/execute nested+quoted; one root\n  reference across all four hosts; parked `(+ <hole> 0.5)` continuation resumes\n  to float64 `2.0` after CBOR round-trip; JVM-side prelude audit finds zero\n  bare integral Double constants.\n- Gate 6: genuine pre-fix c1-2 legacy bytes are embedded AND matched against\n  disk files (SHA-256 `71dc9329…` / `ffb9db68…` verified on disk, sizes\n  1415/1390); they load/execute without recompilation keeping historical\n  meaning (JVM float64 1.0, Node integer 1); recompiling from source under c1-3\n  is distinct from the pre-fix Node artifact.\n- Gate 7: `c1-3` revision + `constructed-collections-float-kind-v1` +\n  `c1-float-kind` profile + accurate `:source-text` (JVM/Node) vs\n  `:forms-only` (Dart/Jolt) capability; C1 marker `1`, SPI `1`, and\n  Python/PHP revision pins unchanged; forms-only hosts refuse direct\n  source reading honestly.\n\n## 5. Migration hazards — CONFIRMED\n\nNo codec change (`dao.jing.cbor`, `dao.host.integer`, `dao.host.number`), no\nVM-equality change (`yin.vm.data`), no C1/marker change, no global\n`yin.vm/primitives` mutation. `constructed-collections-legacy-c1-1.cbor` and the\n`cc4-replay-*` artifacts are present and not in the fix diff (timestamps\n07:59). Pre-fix c1-2 captures carry `manifest-revision \"c1-2\"` and the recorded\nroots, i.e. genuine pre-fix bytes, not artifacts synthesized by the new compiler.\n\n## 6. Honesty — CONFIRMED (with D-1 below)\n\nThe Jolt `yin.vm.data-test` 3 errors are the pre-existing Chez unpaired-surrogate\nlimitation (`:jolt/unimplemented dao.host.text/units->string`), documented in\nthe `src/jolt/dao/host/text.jolt` docstring (\"J1 stopped on that entry\") and in\nprior Jolt round logs (`collab/jolt/1795114000000-engineer-p1c-r3…`), unrelated\nto this round. No skipped host is labeled pass: Dart/Jolt Gate 1/2/REPL tests\nare `(when repl-route? …)`-guarded skips, and the honest `:forms-only` refusal\nis itself asserted in Gate 7.\n\n## Findings / dispositions\n\n**D-1 (non-blocking, evidence hygiene).** `green-jvm-regressions.log` is not a\nclean green run: it shows `311 tests / 3659 assertions / 7 failures, 0 errors`\n— 3 in `yang.clojure-test/indexing-reader-injects-nested-source-positions`\n(source-position injection not yet landed at capture time) and 4 in\n`yin.repl-test/a-host-function-renders-as-a-named-portable-marker` (`=` vs `==`\nrendering). The findings table's \"154 tests / 2,395 assertions / 0 failures\"\nfigure is arithmetically the 10-oracle-namespace subset of that run, and the\ntwo fixes are separately re-verified clean in `green-jvm-repl-clojure.log`\n(157 tests / 1264 assertions / 0 failures, captured later). *Disposition:*\nbefore publication, re-run the JVM regression-oracle set and replace the stale\nlog with a clean one (or mark it stale and cite the clean re-verification).\nThe underlying code is verified green; no rework required.\n\n**D-2 (trivial).** `test/yang/clojure_float_kind_test.cljc` requires\n`clojure.string` but never uses it (kondo warning, not an error). Remove the\nunused require at the next touch.\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":137,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":152576,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f2c1e4a-7b3d-4e8f-a6c5-d0e9f8a1b2c3","uuid":"d85ac5f0-6f78-4a0a-b7fe-00e34e2daebd","timestamp":"2026-11-26T15:37:27.773Z"}
